# C Module Conventions

Every module is a `.h` + `.c` pair in `daemon/src/`.

## Header guard

Use `SPARK_` prefix:

```c
#ifndef SPARK_LOG_H
#define SPARK_LOG_H

/* declarations */

#endif
```

## Include order

1. Own header (in `.c` file)
2. Standard library headers
3. Project headers

## Naming

- Functions: `spark_log_init`, `spark_log_info` (prefix with `spark_<module>_`)
- Types: `spark_log_level_t` (typedef with `_t` suffix)
- Enums: `SPARK_LOG_DEBUG` (uppercase with `SPARK_` prefix)
- Macros: `SPARK_LOG_H` (uppercase with `SPARK_` prefix)
- Internal/static functions: no prefix required

## Style

- C17 standard (`-std=c17`)
- Braces on own line for functions, same line for control flow
- 4-space indent, no tabs
- `snake_case` for all C identifiers
- Keep functions short and focused

## Module template

```c
/* log.h */
#ifndef SPARK_LOG_H
#define SPARK_LOG_H

void spark_log_init(void);

#endif
```

```c
/* log.c */
#include "log.h"

#include <stdio.h>

void spark_log_init(void)
{
    /* ... */
}
```
